    <string name="privacy_text">Tapspend collects no data. No accounts, no analytics, no ads.\n\nIt has no INTERNET permission, so nothing can leave your phone.\n\nWith auto-capture on, it reads bank and card alert SMS (bank sender IDs only) and payment-app notifications. Each alert is parsed on the phone; only the amount, merchant, card or account (last 4 digits), time and reference are kept. The message text is never stored.\n\nYou can turn off SMS and notification access any time in Android settings.</string>
    <string name="quick_tap_tip">On a Pixel? Go to Settings → System → Gestures → Quick Tap → Open app, then choose this app (pick the \"Log expense\" shortcut if offered).</string>
